<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  A-18  settings/perapp - Прокси по приложениям.  H3 · R1.
  24-tab-conformance.md A-18, 00-rules.md 4.5 / 4.8 / 15.
  ============================================================================

  What this replaces: two switches inside a card - one of them with a second,
  independent info target that fired a Toasty - above a GridLayoutManager of bordered
  cards, each with a bare MaterialCheckBox, a `** ` prefix glued onto system app names
  in Kotlin, an 18dp radius, 15sp and 12sp inline sizes, and no empty state, no
  loading state and no search anywhere on screen.

  The screen now reads top to bottom as one ledger (R1):

      §7 header                        «Прокси по приложениям» + one overflow
      Row.Value «Режим»                opens the select popup on Все / Только выбранные /
                                       Кроме выбранных, with the current one marked
      search 56                        filters in place, never navigates
      meta line                        «Отмечено 4 из 128», Caption, Numeric figures
      grouped list                     «Ваши приложения» then «Системные приложения»,
                                       one checkbox row per app, the row owns the box

  Three states share the frame below the meta line and exactly one is visible at a
  time: the list, the skeleton (the package manager is slow on a cold start and the
  screen used to show nothing at all while it worked), and the empty state, which
  carries either «Ничего не найдено» for a search that matched nothing or the load
  failure with «Повторить».

  2026-08 REDESIGN (handoff README §7): the sub-page lekalo header, @layout/view_sub_header.

  THE APP LIST IS ROWS, NOT ONE CARD PER APP. Until this pass every app was its own
  MaterialCardView with a 4dp margin, so 128 apps drew 128 bordered boxes — the one
  composition the prototype never uses anywhere. They are rows with a full-width
  hairline between them now (@layout/view_row_line), which is §6's «строка» exactly.

  THE LIST IS STILL NOT WRAPPED IN A CARD, and that part is a considered departure.
  §7 draws «список приложений с чекбоксами» inside one card, which is right for the
  five demo apps the prototype holds; this list is 128 rows long, scrolls the rest of
  the screen, carries two section headers inside it («Ваши» / «Системные») and shares
  its frame with a skeleton and an empty state. A card around a full-height scrolling
  list draws a boundary that never closes. The mode group above it is the card §7
  asks for, and the rows below read as its continuation.

  THE CHECKBOX IS THE PROTOTYPE'S CONTROL. Each app carries the 22dp box of
  @drawable/bg_checkbox rather than a switch: a switch says «this is on now», a box
  says «this one is in the set», and the set is what the mode row acts on.

  «Российские приложения» (@id/row_ru_preset) STAYS. It is not in §7's table
  because handler/RussianAppsPreset.kt did not exist when the handoff was drawn; the
  owner has named it explicitly as a feature that keeps working.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="?android:attr/colorBackground"
    android:fitsSystemWindows="true"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    tools:context=".ui.PerAppProxyActivity">

    <include
        android:id="@+id/toolbar"
        layout="@layout/view_sub_header" />

    <!-- The mode sits in a card, as the two switches it replaced did at 5e8cd54
         (container_per_app_proxy / container_bypass_apps lived inside one bordered
         card). Owner decision, 2026-08-02: sub-screen content goes back to the
         grouped-card composition; the shared toolbar above stays.

         «Режим» opens §6's select popup, so this card must NOT clip its children or
         the flyout is sliced off at its bottom edge (§11 grabl 4). With the clip gone
         the card stops trimming its first and last row to its own radius, so those two
         carry the corner themselves — see PerAppProxyActivity.bindModeRow. -->
    <com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView
        style="@style/Widget.Departament.CardSection"
        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/screen_gutter"
        android:clipChildren="false"
        android:clipToPadding="false">

        <LinearLayout
            style="@style/Widget.Departament.CardSection.Body"
            android:clipChildren="false"
            android:clipToPadding="false">

            <include
                android:id="@+id/row_mode"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                layout="@layout/view_row" />

            <!-- §6: «Разделитель во всю ширину карточки». -->
            <com.google.android.material.divider.MaterialDivider
                style="@style/Widget.Departament.Divider.Full"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content" />

            <!-- «Российские приложения» — the named bypass preset, in the same card as the
                 mode it depends on, because it is a shortcut for filling that mode's list
                 and reads as a stray feature anywhere else. A plain row with a switch: the
                 whole row is the target, and the contents are one tap away in the actions
                 sheet, which filters the list below to exactly this set. -->
            <include
                android:id="@+id/row_ru_preset"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                layout="@layout/view_row" />
        </LinearLayout>
    </com.google.android.material.card.MaterialCardView>

    <FrameLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
        android:paddingTop="@dimen/space_12"
        android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter">

        <include
            android:id="@+id/search"
            layout="@layout/view_search_field" />
    </FrameLayout>

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/tv_meta"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
        android:layout_marginBottom="@dimen/space_8"
        android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
        android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption"
        tools:text="Отмечено 4 из 128" />

    <!-- ONE of the three children below is visible at a time (00-rules.md 15). -->
    <FrameLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="0dp"
        android:layout_weight="1">

        <androidx.recyclerview.widget.RecyclerView
            android:id="@+id/recycler_view"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="match_parent"
            android:clipToPadding="false"
            android:paddingBottom="@dimen/space_32"
            android:scrollbars="vertical"
            tools:listitem="@layout/view_row_line" />

        <!-- The silhouette of the list, not a spinner over a blank screen: same tile,
             same 68 text origin, same 56 minimum. Shown only after 300ms. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/skeleton"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:importantForAccessibility="noHideDescendants"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:visibility="gone">

            <include
                android:id="@+id/skeleton_1"
                layout="@layout/view_skeleton_row" />

            <include
                android:id="@+id/skeleton_2"
                layout="@layout/view_skeleton_row" />

            <include
                android:id="@+id/skeleton_3"
                layout="@layout/view_skeleton_row" />

            <include
                android:id="@+id/skeleton_4"
                layout="@layout/view_skeleton_row" />

            <include
                android:id="@+id/skeleton_5"
                layout="@layout/view_skeleton_row" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <include
            android:id="@+id/empty_state"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_gravity="center_vertical"
            layout="@layout/view_empty_state" />
    </FrameLayout>
</LinearLayout>
